WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.435
-Good evening, everybody.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.803
This is "Late Night."
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.138
And now, if you don't mind,
we're getting to the news.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:08.107
WNBA star Brittney Griner was
released today

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:10.744
from a Russian prison
in exchange for

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:12.445
an international arm dealer.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.647
It's the first time
the U.S. has traded

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.649
an alleged weed smoker

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:20.119
for an international criminal
since 2016.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.389
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:24.524
President Biden tweeted this
morning

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.992
about the release of WNBA
star Brittney Griner

00:00:26.992 --> 00:00:29.829
from a Russian prison
and said, "She is safe,

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:32.531
she is on a plane,
she is on her way home

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:34.067
and I'd say she's happy,

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:37.704
but she's still a 6'9" person
on a plane."

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.806
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:42.341
Former President Trump's legal
team reportedly found at least

00:00:42.341 --> 00:00:45.044
two items marked classified
while searching through

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:47.013
one of his
Florida storage units,

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.115
and that's not all they found.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:53.686
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.655
"I'm having trouble
with my rent."

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:58.557
That's right.

00:00:58.557 --> 00:01:00.026
Trump's legal team
reportedly found at least

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.361
two items marked classified

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.295
in one of his storage units
in West Palm Beach.

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.098
You needed a storage unit?

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:07.099
How many documents
did you steal?

00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:09.769
You live in a hotel.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.337
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.105
For the first time in four
decades,

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:15.608
journalists and staffers at
'The New York Times" last night

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.777
began a 24-hour strike
to protest

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.245
for better salaries
and benefits,

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:22.348
so for today only
there were two reasons

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:25.451
why posting your Wordle score
makes you a jerk.

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:29.621
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.621 --> 00:01:31.157
According to a new study,

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.558
it takes
the average American worker

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:33.859
one year and seven months

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:36.095
to feel like they're thriving
in a new job.

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.397
Here's the study.

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:42.201
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:43.702
Oprah recently released

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:45.905
the annual list
of her favorite things.

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.807
Coming in at number one,
creating a monster!

00:01:48.807 --> 00:01:50.810
[ Laughter, groaning ]

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.779
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:55.348
Firefighters recently rescued

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:58.317
a puppy that swam about
a mile across the Hudson River

00:01:58.317 --> 00:01:59.885
from Manhattan to New Jersey.

00:01:59.885 --> 00:02:00.987
They tried to return it,

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.955
but it had already found
an affordable home

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:04.824
with a backyard
and started a family.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:07.593
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:10.062
The appliance company Dyson
is set to launch

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:12.131
a set of noise canceling
headphones

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:14.233
with a detachable air purifier.

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:16.703
It's part of Dyson's
long-time mission

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.973
of trying to figure out what
the hell their company sells.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.941
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.810
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.613
"Headph-- Headphones?"

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.315
And finally, Google released

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:32.285
its annual year-end
search list yesterday,

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:35.655
and the most searched TV show
in the U.S. was "Euphoria,"

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:37.456
as in,
"Where can I get the drugs

00:02:37.456 --> 00:02:40.059
they were doing
in last night's 'Euphoria'?"

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.428
And that was the monologue,
everybody!

